    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4fd30e7e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: i_hate_when_i_see_a_black_out_in_my_neighborhood_but_i_still_offer_my_neighbors_a_candle; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man in a Ku Klux Klan-style robe and hood, juxtaposed with text that expresses hatred toward Black people ('I hate when I see a black out in my neighborhood') while simultaneously offering a 'candle' — a symbol of appeasement or passive tolerance. The visual of the KKK imagery directly maps onto the hateful sentiment expressed in the text, creating an analogical link between the wearer's identity and the racist message. The meme is designed to convey and reinforce anti-Black racism by using the KKK as a symbol of white supremacist hate, while the 'offering a candle' is a sarcastic or ironic gesture that implies a false sense of moral superiority or reconciliation. This is a hateful meme because it directly targets Black people through racist stereotypes and imagery, and it promotes a hostile, exclusionary worldview. The overall intent is to normalize or justify racial hatred under the guise of 'offering help,' which is a form of hate speech and harmful propaganda.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_21daa678"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
